# seat-ui — round 7 working notes (write-as-you-go)

Seat: UI composition. Build: commit 984a0f17, frozen.

## F1 (confirmed by measurement) — the board's right margin is 110px of dead white at 1920

`.board` is `display:grid` with `grid-template-columns: 372px 372px 372px 172px 372px`
at 1920 (measured). Full lanes clamp at 372px; the empty WAITING lane collapses to
`var(--rail)` = 172px (deliberate, documented at _gate-suite.html:1833-1841). The 200px
that collapse hands back is never redistributed.

Measured, viewport → (board content right, last tray right, gap):
- 1810 → 1776 / 1776 / **0**
- 1850 → 1816 / 1776 / **40**
- 1920 → 1886 / 1776 / **110**   ← the canonical shot width
- 2048 → 1995 / 1795 / **200**
- 2560 → 2251 / 2051 / **200** (capped: the sheet's own max-width takes over)

tasks.dense (no empty lane) fills to the content edge at every width — gap 0 everywhere.
So the defect is specific to the shipped board state, which is exactly the state that is
screenshotted, demoed and shown to Orla.

Consequence: at 1920 the board's own optical margins are 16px left / 126px right.

### F1 alignment contract (measured, tasks.board, .headActions right vs last card right)
| vw | head/Show right | last card right | break |
|---|---|---|---|
|1280|1234|1234|0|
|1440|1394|1394|0|
|1600|1554|1554|0|
|1750|1704|1704|0|
|1810|1764|1764|0|
|1850|1804|1764|**40**|
|1920|1874|1764|**110**|
|2048|1983|1783|**200**|

Left edge (wordmark ↔ first card) is 128 at every width — perfect. So the surface
holds a single right-hand edge from 1280 to 1810 and abandons it above.
Notes (head 1561 = paperStack 1531 + inset, stack centred on sheet centre 1001) and
Timeline (tl-stage centred, 140→1862) both stay centred at 1920. Only Tasks drifts.
Second-order: the dock is centred on the SHEET (816.1→1185.9, centre 1001) but the
board's occupied area is 116→1776, centre 946 — so at 1920 the one floating object on
the sheet sits 55px off the optical centre of the thing it floats over.

The CSS's own comment (line ~1805) states the intent: "An empty lane on a populated
board is a rail rather than a fifth of the sheet ... **and the four lanes with work in
them take the room**." Above 1810 they do not; the room becomes dead white.

FIX, verified by injection — one declaration beside the five existing `:has()` rules:
```css
[data-app="tasks"] .board:not([data-filtered]):not([data-blank]):has(> .tray[data-empty]) {
  --lane: minmax(196px, 422px);   /* 372 + (372-172)/4 */
}
```
Measured after injection: break 0 at 1200/1280/1440/1810/1920/2048/2560; no new
horizontal scroll at any width; tracks at 1920 become 399.5 399.5 399.5 172 399.5.

## F2 (confirmed by screenshot + measurement) — the list's last row is eaten by the dock

`.board.listBoard` reserves `padding-bottom: 28px`. `.board` (the card board) reserves
`padding: 0 16px 84px`. The dock is 48px tall sitting 18px off the sheet's foot, so its
band is 66px + shadow. 28px is not enough.

At 768x1000, tasks.board (the LIST is the view below 1199), scrolled to the true end of
the scroller (scrollTop = scrollHeight, nothing further to reveal):
- dock band  y 922 → 970, x 237 → 607
- last row   y 917 → 953  ("Send registrar paperwork two weeks before the date")
The final task's title and its owner's name sit entirely inside the dock's box. Screenshot
_zz-list-end-768.png shows the tick, the DONE pip and the 2 Jul pill surviving either side
of the dock with the person's words gone.

Reproduced identically at 900x1000. Board states at 1280/1920 are clean (84px reserve).
Notes is clean at 390/768/1280/1920.

## F3 (confirmed by driving) — the list's tick column never paints its own done state

`.tick` base (line ~2051): `color: transparent`, `box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1.4px var(--ink-4)`.
The fill lives at line 2326 and is scoped to the CARD only:
`[data-app="tasks"] .card[data-done] .tick { background: var(--ink); box-shadow: none; color: var(--white); }`
There is no `.lrow[data-done] .tick` counterpart. The list has `.lrow[data-done] .lrowTitle`
and `.lrowNote` colour rules (1723-1724) and nothing else.

Measured at 1024x900, all 13 rows, 8 open + 5 done:
- tick background: `rgba(0,0,0,0)` on ALL 13
- tick ring: `rgba(17,17,17,0.28) 0 0 0 1.4px inset` on ALL 13
- check glyph colour: `rgba(0,0,0,0)` on ALL 13
- aria-checked: false×8 / true×5
The only painted difference on a done row is the title going `rgb(17,17,17)` →
`rgba(17,17,17,0.62)`.

Driven: clicked an open row's tick at 1024. `data-done` flips, the lane word becomes
DONE, the pip goes green, the title fades — and the circle under the pointer stays an
empty ring (`_zz-tick-post.png`). `.card[data-just-done] .tick` carries the settle
animation and the check-draw; `.lrow` has no equivalent, so there is no moment of
completion at all in the list.

The behaviour gate asserts `after.done` — the ATTRIBUTE flipped (interaction-check.mjs:314).
It never asserts the control paints. So this is not a restatement.
The card's own comment (2320) claims done is said "four times over ... and the filled
tick". In the list one of those four survives.

Affects every width from 320 to 1199, where the list is the default view — Orla's laptop
and her iPad — and the phone, where the list is the ONLY view.

FIX (mirror the two card rules; verified by injection, `_zz-tick-list-fixed.png`):
```css
[data-app="tasks"] .card[data-done] .tick,
[data-app="tasks"] .lrow[data-done] .tick { background: var(--ink); box-shadow: none; color: var(--white); }
[data-app="tasks"] .card[data-done] .tick:hover, [data-app="tasks"] .card[data-done] .tick:focus-visible,
[data-app="tasks"] .lrow[data-done] .tick:hover, [data-app="tasks"] .lrow[data-done] .tick:focus-visible { box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px var(--wash-2); }
```
Palette-safe (--ink on white, --white glyph — the exact pair the card already ships).

## F4 (measured) — the Timeline carries two indigo hairlines and only one is a measure

Census of every horizontal rule on timeline.desk @1920 (computed colours):
- `.tl-paperEdge`  x140→1862  `rgba(17,17,17,0.16)`
- `.b-behind`      x197→1805  `rgba(17,17,17,0.16)`
- `.b-foot`        x197→1805  `rgba(17,17,17,0.16)`
- `.b-todayRule`   x449→793   **`rgb(79,70,229)`**  — 344px, `max-width:344px`, IDENTICAL at 1280/1440/1920
- `.b-rail`        x201→1801  **`rgb(79,70,229)`**  — the measure; 1120 @1440, 1600 @1920

Every divider on the page is ink-16 except one, and that one is the accent, 1px, horizontal,
265px directly above the measure, in the same colour and weight. On a surface whose stated
organising principle is that horizontal length is `daysFromToday × pixels-per-day`, a second
accent hairline of a length that means nothing — and that never moves while the measure
below it grows by 480px — invites exactly the wrong reading. (Down layout is clean: the
measure is vertical there, so the two never compete. This is an `across` defect.)

FIX: `[data-app="timeline"] .b-todayRule { background: var(--fore-16); }` (line 6592) — the
same ink tint the page's other three rules already use. One indigo line remains and it is
the measure. In-palette, no new hue.

## F5 (measured, fix verified) — the phone's list does not sit on the head's column

Tasks, list view. Head content edge vs list leading edge:
| vw | wordmark L | tick L | Δ | head actions R | row meta R | Δ |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
|768 |116|117|1|728|728|0|
|1024|128|129|1|978|978|0|
|1199|128|129|1|1153|1153|0|
|**390**|25|**40**|**15**|365|**350**|**15**|
|430 |25|40|15|405|390|15|
|600 |25|40|15|575|560|15|
The desk keeps the contract to a pixel; the phone breaks it by 15px on both sides, because
the head's inset drops 28→16 under 720 while `.board.listBoard { padding: 0 25px }` is never
re-scoped. On a 390px screen the whole list sits 15px inside the wordmark, project name,
progress line and segmented control stacked above it.

FIX (verified at 320/390/430/600; desk untouched, no horizontal scroll anywhere):
```css
@media (max-width: 720px) {
  [data-app="tasks"] .board.listBoard { padding-left: 10px; padding-right: 10px; }
}
```
After: tick L = 25 = wordmark L; row meta R = 365 = head actions R, at every phone width.

## Checked and CLEAN (not findings)
- Sheet geometry identical in all three products at 1920: 100/18/18/18. Dock centred on the
  sheet's centre to the pixel (816.1→1185.9, centre 1001 = sheet centre 1001).
- Notes' 1120 stack and 1060 paper are centred on 1001; Timeline's stage 140→1862 centred
  on 1001. Only Tasks' board drifts (F1).
- Rail capsule: 10px top inset, 10px bottom inset, 10px either side of every tile, avatar
  centred to the pixel at every width tested.
- Resize round trip 1440→1200→…→390→…→1440 in all three products: head, views, board, dock,
  seg, tools, headActions and every tray width restore EXACTLY. Zero page errors.
- Planning drawer at 1920: board refills to gap 0; at 1440 it becomes a scroller rather
  than dropping Done. Both correct.
- Timeline moment labels: fixed 168px boxes alternating above/below, no same-side collision
  at 1920; the copy block keeps reading order on both sides (a mirror of the BLOCK, which is
  right — I checked and dropped this as a finding).
- Dense board @1920: five equal 354px lanes filling the sheet exactly, fold rule + count per
  lane. This is the proof that the board's grid is capable of what F1 asks for.
